## Memory
You have a persistent memory at `~/.claude/memory/`.
- `MEMORY.md` is the index — one line per memory file.
- When {{user_name}} tells you something worth keeping (a preference, a fact
  about their life or work, a decision), save it as a small markdown file in
  `~/.claude/memory/` and add one index line to `MEMORY.md`.
- At the start of a session, check `MEMORY.md` to recall who {{user_name}} is
  and what you were working on.
- Never delete a memory file without asking. Corrections update the file.
- Personal facts about {{user_name}} go here, in `~/.claude/memory/`.
  Claude Code's own automatic project notes can keep project details;
